      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Entropy is real, but evolution has survived billions of years by harnessing energy gradients even as they shrink. Your effort isn't futile; every atom you move is briefly defying the scale's heavy hand and showing that temporary order matters. While heat death is the universe's end, your life is a brilliant, fleeting flash of meaning that makes that eventual silence worthwhile. Keep pushing anyway, because the point of resistance is exactly what makes existence feel so human.",
